hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1641","**\nNarrated to us Muhammad ibn al-'Ala' ibn Kuraib, who said: Narrated to us Abu Khalid, who informed us al-Husayn al-Muktab.\n\nAlso, narrated to us 'Ali ibn Khashram, who said: Narrated to us 'Isa, from al-Husayn.\n\nAlso, narrated to us Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Masruqi, who said: Narrated to us Abu Usamah, from al-Husayn, from 'Amr ibn Shu'ayb, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, the freed slave of Maymunah, who said:\nI came upon Ibn 'Umar while he was sitting on the *balat* (stone platform), and the people were in prayer. So I said: \Will you not pray?\"" He said: \""I have already prayed.\"" I said: \""Will you not pray with them?\"" He said: \""Indeed"," I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: 'Do not pray a prayer twice in one day.'\""\n\nThis is the narration of 'Isa."""
